Package: rdp-usb-gw
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: kmod, systemd, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: USB redirection for Linux RDP servers
 rdp-usb-gw implements the server side of RDP USB redirection (MS-RDPEUSB,
 the URBDRC dynamic channel). Devices an RDP client redirects, such as a
 security key, appear on the Linux machine as local devices, attached through
 USB/IP's vhci_hcd.
 .
 It doesn't speak RDP. The RDP server lends it the session's URBDRC channels
 over a unix socket, so the server needs a small proxy for it, such as the
 one in gnome-remote-desktop from the grd-with-usb-redirect packages.
 .
 vhci_hcd is in the linux-modules-extra package on Ubuntu.
